{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_013ygzWUBWn77KTbQ7kE4uwH", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_Havana\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/cuba/havana/centro-habana/attractions/old-city-wall/a/poi-sig/370297/1341262\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.geographicus.com/P/RareMaps/siscarajuan\"}, {\"url\": \"https://havanatimes.org/?p=153635\"}, {\"url\": \"https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Havana\"}, {\"url\": \"https://cubadecentel.com/havanaENG/muralla_de_la_habana/muralla_de_la_habanaENG1.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://deinospoesia.com/2024/12/03/colonial-cuba-an-exhibition/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.geographicus.com/P/RareMaps/siscarajuan_sold\"}, {\"url\": \"https://EN.wikipedia.com/wiki/Habana\"}, {\"url\": \"https://newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Old_Havana\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:31:48.255Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Havana city walls begun 1674 by 1690s surrounded the city completed", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01K4XQzRnsr7gkZN1GR4V6Bd", "content": [{"title": "Timeline of Havana", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_Havana"}, {"title": "Old City Wall", "url": "https://www.lonelyplanet.com/cuba/havana/centro-habana/attractions/old-city-wall/a/poi-sig/370297/1341262"}, {"title": "www.geographicus.com", "url": "https://www.geographicus.com/P/RareMaps/siscarajuan"}, {"title": "Havana’s El Prado Promenade", "url": "https://havanatimes.org/?p=153635"}, {"title": "www.wikipedia.org", "url": "https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Havana"}, {"title": "muralla de la habanaENG1", "url": "https://cubadecentel.com/havanaENG/muralla_de_la_habana/muralla_de_la_habanaENG1.htm"}, {"title": "colonial cuba an exhibition", "url": "https://deinospoesia.com/2024/12/03/colonial-cuba-an-exhibition/"}, {"title": "siscarajuan sold", "url": "https://www.geographicus.com/P/RareMaps/siscarajuan_sold"}, {"title": "en.wikipedia.com", "url": "https://EN.wikipedia.com/wiki/Habana"}, {"title": "Old Havana", "url": "https://newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Old_Havana"}]}, "Sources broadly agree that construction began in 1674, but they disagree on when it finished. Some suggest the landward side was largely done by the 1690s, while others date full completion to the 1740s or 1790s.\n\n- **Start date:** Construction began in 1674 under the engineer Juan de Siscara, according to a Cuban historical account. A Geographicus biography of Siscara says the harbor-facing wall was finished in 1680 and that by 1688 the land-facing wall, separating the city from its suburbs, was included.\n- **Land side in the 1690s:** A different account says the land part was completed in 1698, and then the bay part in 1740. This partly supports your premise, though the dates for the landward wall differ (1688 versus 1698).\n- **Full completion:** Estimates vary. Wikipedia's Havana article says the walls were started in 1674 as part of the fortification efforts and would be completed by 1740. Other sources give 1797. The Rockford University exhibit says construction extended for more than 100 years, until 1797, when the section facing Havana Bay was completed, and New World Encyclopedia gives 1674 to 1797. One account notes that the 1797 date when some moats are added.\n- **Demolition:** Demolition began in 1863 (per the Rockford exhibit and Lonely Planet).\n\nIn short, the walls were begun in 1674 and the landward side was largely finished by the late 1600s, but the whole circuit was not finished until the 18th century, with some sources placing the end in 1740 and others in 1797."], "durationSeconds": 6.595380916, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_013ygzWUBWn77KTbQ7kE4uwH", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
